{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_b75920c89206e8abc5e0d46a940a641afdf0ba8908586cdb712fcf0dc7dfe8fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"iosm-spec.md is a normative specification of the IOSM (Improve, Optimize, Shrink, Modularize) methodology, defining ordered phases, quality gates, normalized metrics, evidence-confidence rules, and an aggregate IOSM-Index score."}],"claim_ids":["clm_b75920c89206e8abc5e0d46a940a641afdf0ba8908586cdb712fcf0dc7dfe8fd"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:12:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_49e3eb9d9c6f43ab8c47562957454f04","id":"pg_9a7090abcef95559bb0febc617397d45","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/rokoss21-iosm-cli-iosm-spec-md-6cb971ca9c23-ebc617397d45.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6c3b6c944a3f54428c513ea1b99cf934"],"title":"rokoss21/iosm-cli/iosm-spec.md @ 6cb971ca9c23","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:12:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49e3eb9d9c6f43ab8c47562957454f04"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_681652bc83cda90b4f779bd6c102b5f44ae1b049b6f42ecc42ed186913c08dd3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Extension tools can declare permission tiers (read-only, workspace-write, danger-full-access); with permissions.extensionToolEnforcement=true, read-only extension tools run automatically in auto mode and tools lacking requiredPermission metadata are blocked there."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87cae113a1c3c5204a6909af3016baaaf4afc920614b36a75d5cfc75677876e9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Settings merge later-wins: global ~/.iosm/agent/settings.json lowest priority, then project .iosm/settings.json, then CLI flags at highest priority."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c1edaa8f67958d6ec4f988e69f8d9fd8b156d9a720a67484bc02df5c1fca6a46"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Profiles control behavior and available tools: full grants all built-ins, plan is a read-only bundle, iosm adds IOSM cycle context, and meta is orchestration-first for multi-agent delegation; db_run is enabled only in write-capable profiles (full, meta, iosm)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_feda1eb8196f0b2bae19da4afe24bd56939ec1b9d03740ef44cc854177f653fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions persist under ~/.iosm/agent/sessions with JSONL trace files in session-traces; semantic search indexes are cached per project hash under ~/.iosm/agent/semantic/indexes containing meta.json, chunks.jsonl, and vectors.jsonl."}],"claim_ids":["clm_681652bc83cda90b4f779bd6c102b5f44ae1b049b6f42ecc42ed186913c08dd3","clm_87cae113a1c3c5204a6909af3016baaaf4afc920614b36a75d5cfc75677876e9","clm_c1edaa8f67958d6ec4f988e69f8d9fd8b156d9a720a67484bc02df5c1fca6a46","clm_feda1eb8196f0b2bae19da4afe24bd56939ec1b9d03740ef44cc854177f653fe"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:12:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_49e3eb9d9c6f43ab8c47562957454f04","id":"pg_c58fe52152625070b599b4a101a79026","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/rokoss21-iosm-cli-docs-configuration-md-6cb971ca9c23-b4a101a79026.